    "name": "AthenaVI Backend",
    "description": "API collection for AthenaVI_backend. Default `baseUrl` is `http://localhost:9000` (see `PORT` in `.env`).\n\n**Auth:** Protected routes use `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`. Run **Login** or **Register** first; the test script saves `accessToken` to collection variables.\n\n**Refresh / Logout:** These use the `refreshToken` **httpOnly** cookie. In Postman, enable the cookie jar (default on) and run Login so cookies are stored for `baseUrl`.\n\n**Multipart:** Workspace asset upload and profile image use `form-data` with the field names shown on each request.\n\n**HeyGen avatar videos** live under **Workspaces → HeyGen videos (project)**. They require workspace **OWNER, ADMIN, or MEMBER** and a valid `projectId` in that workspace. Set `workspaceId`, `projectId`, and (for create) real `avatarId` / `voiceId` from HeyGen list endpoints. **Create** saves `heygenVideoId` to collection variables when the response is 201.\n\n**HeyGen (v3 proxy)** under **HeyGen**: with **`ownership=private`** / **`type=private`**, the backend filters HeyGen list responses **after** the upstream call (handles varying JSON shapes such as nested **`data`** arrays). Only rows tied to **your** user in `heygen_avatars` / `heygen_voices` are returned. Run **Create avatar** to capture `groupId`; **Design voice** / **Clone a voice** to capture `voiceId`. Consent and GET voice-by-id enforce ownership (**403** if another user's recorded asset).",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
